    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a potent offensive outlook, anchored by the high-ceiling production of **Yordan Alvarez** (82.97) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (80.98). **Yordan Alvarez** remains our premier start, leveraging an elite 0.469 xwOBA against Quantrill to provide a massive floor, while **Pete Crow-Armstrong** benefits from a favorable matchup against Greene. Although **Pete Crow-Armstrong** carries a 35% rain risk, his dynamic platoon advantage (+14%) and leadoff spot make him an essential play for our pursuit of scarce stolen bases. **Trea Turner** also projects as a strong engine for our 5x5 categories, benefiting from a move to the #1 hole and a solid matchup against Flaherty, further bolstered by the Zebras\u2019 focus on maximizing sprint speed efficiency.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involved **Carson Benge** (50.02), who narrowly missed the cut behind the more efficient profiles of **Casey Schmitt** and **Luke Raley**. While **Carson Benge** offered some platoon utility, his marginal score was suppressed by a challenging matchup against Gray and a 36% rain risk, ultimately failing to displace the higher-rated **Junior Caminero** (65.48) in the utility slot. We are monitoring **Christian Yelich** closely; despite a sub-60 score (54.64), his leadoff position and platoon edge against Ashcraft keep him in the lineup, though we are prepared to pivot if the weather forecast for **Pete Crow-Armstrong** deteriorates, potentially sliding **Carson Benge** or **Caleb Durbin** into the utility role if necessary. We continue to hold **Hyeseong Kim** in the minors, waiting for a roster vacancy to utilize his speed profile in the future.",
